<!-- 2. L'APPROCHE -->
<section class="section" id="approche">
  <div class="grille">
    <img class="photo photo-teinte format-4-3 grille-a" src="/images/yoga-cours-1000.webp" srcset="/images/yoga-cours-1000.webp 1000w, /images/yoga-cours-2000.webp 2000w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 38vw" width="2000" height="1500" alt="Group yoga class: four people sitting cross-legged on their mats in the practice's studio" loading="lazy">

    <div class="grille-b">
      <p class="surtitre">The approach</p>
      <h2 class="titre-2">Yoga that is attentive, inclusive and free of performance</h2>
      <p>I have practised yoga since 2013. It has allowed me to trust my body more, to listen to it with kindness and to move without striving for performance.</p>
      <p>I trained in vinyasa yoga at Ayu Yoga School, whose demanding, inclusive and decolonial approach fully matches my values. For prenatal and postnatal yoga, I was trained by Bernadette de Gasquet.</p>
      <p>My work as a physiotherapist also informs every class: I know bodies that are changing, bodies in pain, bodies regaining confidence.</p>
      <ul class="filets">
        <li><strong>Breathing</strong> — it guides every movement and calms the nervous system.</li>
        <li><strong>Adaptation</strong> — the posture adapts to the body, never the other way round.</li>
        <li><strong>Attention</strong> — you focus on what you feel, here and now.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

