<!-- 6. QUESTIONS FRÉQUENTES -->
<section class="section" id="questions">
  <div class="grille">
    <div class="grille-a">
      <h2 class="titre-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p>Hesitating before you start? Here are the questions I am asked most often.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq grille-b">
      <details>
        <summary>I have never done yoga. Is it for me?</summary>
        <p>Yes. The classes are designed to be accessible without experience. I demonstrate each posture, I offer variations and you can stop at any time.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to be flexible?</summary>
        <p>Not at all. Flexibility is neither a starting point nor a goal: the aim is above all to move with more ease and to breathe better.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I practise while pregnant, or just after giving birth?</summary>
        <p>Yes. If in doubt, talk to your doctor or your midwife.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I have back pain. Is that compatible?</summary>
        <p>Most of the time, yes. Let me know at the start of the class so that I can adapt the postures. If the pain is recent or severe, a medical consultation remains the first step.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I book or cancel?</summary>
        <p>Group classes are booked on Doctolib. For a private class, write to me.</p>
        <p>To cancel a group class, go to Doctolib. Otherwise, write to me. A cancellation made up to 24&nbsp;hours before the class is not deducted.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How long are class passes valid?</summary>
        <p>5-class passes are valid for 6&nbsp;months from the date of purchase.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

